schema_id: atlas.hypergraph-expansion-budget
schema_version: 1
schema_kind: resource_budget
status: ACTIVE

description: >
  Finite query-time limits around the existing n-ary HyperGraphRAG traversal.
  The budget limits expansion work; it never rewrites canonical hyperedges into
  binary truth.

fields:
  schema: { type: literal, value: atlas.hypergraph-expansion-budget.v1 }
  maxEdges: { type: integer, minimum: 0 }
  maxMembers: { type: integer, minimum: 0 }
  maxHops: { type: integer, minimum: 0 }
  maxTokens: { type: integer, minimum: 0 }
  maxMillis: { type: integer, minimum: 0 }
  policyRevision: { type: string, required: true }

invariants:
  - expansion stops when any finite bound is exhausted
  - n-ary member roles and edge identity are preserved
  - projection/executor choice does not change canonical relation meaning
